        "answer": "In Series III Faraday tested common and voltaic electricity against five effect classes: tension, magnetic action, chemical decomposition, physiological shock effects, and spark behavior. He found qualitative identity across these domains. In §307 he concluded that common electricity is as magnetic as voltaic electricity when experimental conditions allow sufficient action time, supporting one underlying electrical agency rather than separate kinds."
